# CVE-2024-23342 — ecdsa (transitive via python-jose[cryptography] in backend/requirements.txt)
# The Minerva timing side-channel affects pure-Python ECDSA operations.
# This service uses python-jose only for HS256 (HMAC-SHA256) JWTs with a
# symmetric secret; no ECDSA/elliptic-curve code path is exercised, so the
# vulnerable operation is unreachable in this codebase. Upstream python-ecdsa
# considers side-channel resistance out of scope and has issued no fix, so the
# finding cannot be remediated by a version bump.
# Owner: @damienjburks. Re-evaluate if the backend adopts ECDSA/ES* JWT
# algorithms, or when python-ecdsa ships a fix / python-jose drops the ecdsa dependency.
# See: https://github.com/devsecblueprint/devsecblueprint/issues/175
CVE-2024-23342
